hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"990","1025 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding: To all We appointed heirs. He said: Heirs. And regarding: As for those with whom you made pledges, give them their share. He said: When the Emigrants came to Madinah, an Emigrant used to inherit from an Ansari to the exclusion of his blood relatives, through the brotherhood the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had established between them. When the verse came down: To all We appointed heirs, it abrogated it. Then he recited: As for those with whom you made pledges, give them their share: of help, counsel, support, and bequest; the inheritance has gone."
"991","1026 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid and Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever, nor the disbeliever from the Muslim."
"992","1027 - al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us. And Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Attach the fixed shares to their rightful owners; what remains belongs to the nearest male relative."
"993","1028 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me, he and Abu Bakr, among Banu Salimah. He found me unconscious, so he called for water, performed ablution, and sprinkled some of it over me. I came to, and said: How should I dispose of my wealth, O Messenger of Allah? Then there came down: Allah instructs you concerning your children: for the male twice the share of the female."
"994","1029 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Hasin, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever leaves wealth, it belongs to his agnates; and whoever leaves a burden or dependents, they come to me, for I am his guardian."
"995","1030 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me, he and Abu Bakr, both walking, while I had lost consciousness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution then poured his ablution water over me. I came to and said: O Messenger of Allah, how should I settle my wealth? How should I dispose of my wealth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer me, until the inheritance verse came down. 1031 - He said: And Abu al-Zubayr said: There came down concerning him: They ask you; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning the kalalah."
"996","1032 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Ishaq ibn Kharashah, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, who said: A grandmother came to Abu Bakr asking him for her inheritance. He said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I know nothing for you in the practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); go back until I ask the people. So he asked the people, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give her a sixth. Abu Bakr said: Is there anyone with you besides you? Then Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari stood and said the like of what al-Mughirah had said, so Abu Bakr granted it to her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, asking him for her inheritance. He said: You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and the judgment that reached us which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave was for other than you. I shall not add anything to the fixed shares; but it is that sixth: if you both share it, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers."
"997","1033 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Abu al-Munib informed us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted the grandmother a sixth, when there is no mother."
"998","1034 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son died; what of his inheritance is mine? He said: A sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him and said: Another sixth for you. When he turned away, he called him and said: The other sixth is a bonus. Qatadah said: The least the grandfather inherits is a sixth, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him a sixth; and we do not know with whom he made him inherit."
"999","1035 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Qays, from al-Huzayl, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning a man who left his daughter, his son's daughter, and his sister: he gave his daughter half, his son's daughter a sixth, and the rest to his sister."
"1000","1036 - Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr, meaning Ibn Shumayl, narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim; al-Aswad said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal judged among us in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a man who left his daughter and his sister. He said: He judged half for his daughter and half for his sister."
"1001","1037 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah: Teach your boys swimming and your fighters archery. They used to compete at targets, when a stray arrow came and killed a boy in the care of a maternal uncle of his, of unknown origin. Abu Ubaydah wrote to Umar: To whom shall I hand his blood-money? Umar wrote, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of whoever has no guardian, and the maternal uncle is the heir of whoever has no heir."
"1002","1038 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Abu Amir al-Hawzani, from al-Miqdam al-Kindi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves a debt or dependents, they come to me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the guardian of whoever has no guardian: I inherit his wealth and ransom his captive. And the maternal uncle is the guardian of whoever has no guardian: he inherits his wealth and ransoms his captive."
"1003","1039 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Blood-money belongs to the paternal kin, and a wife does not inherit from her husband's blood-money, until al-Dahhak al-Kilabi informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to him to grant the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi her share of her husband's blood-money."
"1004","1040 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih informed us, from Umar ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, who said: My father informed me, from my grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: People of two religions do not inherit from one another. A wife inherits from her husband's blood-money and wealth, and he inherits from her blood-money and wealth, unless one of them kills the other. If one of them kills the other, he inherits nothing of his blood-money or wealth; and if one of them kills the other by mistake, he inherits from his wealth but not from his blood-money."
